+## Sales import and variance
+
+- `POST /import/sales` takes `{ "csv": "..." }` with the columns
+  `ticket,soldAt,dishId,qty` (`soldAt` is an ISO instant, `qty` a whole
+  number of dishes). Each dish sold consumes one recipe portion per `qty`,
+  booked in the ledger at `soldAt` with the ref `sale:<ticket>`. The answer is
+  `{ "tickets": 2, "dishes": 5 }`: the tickets imported and the dishes on
+  them (the sum of `qty`). A ticket already in the ledger is skipped.
+  The file is all or nothing: a bad row answers `bad_request` and an item
+  running out answers `sale_not_enough_stock`; both messages name the row
+  (`row 2` is the first data row).
+- `GET /reports/variance?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD` lists, per item with
+  use in those days (inclusive, UTC), `theoretical` (use by sales sold in
+  those days), `actual` (every `consume` movement in those days) and
+  `difference` (actual minus theoretical).
